{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"54998","self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54998","key":"SV-8871","renderedFields":{"statuscategorychangedate":"Yesterday 9:31 AM","issuetype":null,"timespent":null,"project":null,"customfield_10351":"","fixVersions":null,"aggregatetimespent":null,"statusCategory":null,"resolution":null,"resolutiondate":null,"workratio":null,"watches":null,"issuerestriction":null,"lastViewed":"Yesterday 11:52 PM","created":"Yesterday 9:31 AM","customfield_10021":null,"customfield_10385":null,"priority":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10016":null,"customfield_10019":null,"timeestimate":null,"aggregatetimeoriginalestimate":null,"versions":null,"customfield_10418":null,"customfield_10419":null,"issuelinks":null,"assignee":null,"updated":"Today 12:49 PM","status":null,"components":null,"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"Environment\"></a>Environment</h3>\n\n<p>QA branch <a href=\"https://sv8785.qa.shopview.com/workorders\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://sv8785.qa.shopview.com/workorders</a> — build v3.4.2-d00239b (index.html last modified Tue, 04 Aug 2026 22:51:02 GMT). Desktop browser, signed in as an Admin.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"StepstoReproduce\"></a>Steps to Reproduce</h3>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Open Work Orders on the All tab with no filters on.</li>\n\t<li>Click the Customer button and pick the customer named Iibay Landscaping. The button correctly reads \"Customer: Iibay Landscaping\" and the list narrows.</li>\n\t<li>Now leave the page and come back — any of these four does it: open a work order and click back; refresh the page; close the browser completely and sign in again; or open the same link in a new window.</li>\n\t<li>Look at the Customer button.</li>\n\t<li>Repeat the whole thing with the Lead Technician button (pick Admin ShopView) and with the Service Advisor button (pick Admin ShopView).</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"ExpectedResult\"></a>Expected Result</h3>\n\n<p>The button should still read \"Customer: Iibay Landscaping\", the same as it did before you left the page. The user needs to see WHICH customer the list is filtered by without opening the button.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"CurrentResult\"></a>Current Result</h3>\n\n<p>The button comes back blue (switched on) but reads only \"Customer\" — the customer's name is gone. The filter itself is still working: the list is still filtered by that customer, and if you open the button the name is there as a tag with a tick beside it. So the list is filtered by something the screen no longer names.</p>\n\n<p>The same thing happens on the Lead Technician and Service Advisor buttons. It does NOT happen on the Status or Asset on Site buttons — those keep their value (\"Status: Paid\" comes back correctly), so a user sees one button naming its value and another not naming its value side by side.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Howoften\"></a>How often</h3>\n\n<p>Every time, on all four routes back to the page, on all three of those buttons. Reproduced twice from a clean start.</p>\n\n<h3><a name=\"Technicaldetail\"></a>Technical detail</h3>\n\n<p>The three affected filters are the ones whose choices are fetched from the server (/api/customers/list-options and the staff list); the two unaffected ones are fixed lists held in the page. On a restore the saved filter value is read back and applied to the request (filters<span class=\"error\">&#91;n&#93;</span><span class=\"error\">&#91;field&#93;</span>=company_id&amp;filters<span class=\"error\">&#91;n&#93;</span><span class=\"error\">&#91;value&#93;</span>=00122246-ab6d-47ee-a885-3425c7bda754) but the button's label is rendered before the name for that id is available, and is not re-rendered once it arrives. Specification references: S7-R1, which says the chip \"displays the selected value(s)\", and S10-R1, which says filter selections are \"restored exactly as they were left\".</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Filters specification, version 18, requirement S7-R1, which says: \"When a filter has one or more values selected, the chip changes to an active/highlighted visual state (blue pill) and displays the selected value(s)\". The last five words are the part that is missing.</p>\n\n<p>And requirement S10-R1, which says: \"When the user navigates away from the Work Orders page (e.g., to a Work Order detail, then back), the filter selections and collapsed/expanded state are restored exactly as they were left\".</p>","customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/59322","id":"59322","filename":"screen-capture - 2026-08-05T123205.802.webm","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bilal.muzamil@shopview.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png"},"displayName":"Bilal Muzamil","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Karachi","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"Yesterday 12:32 PM","size":"1.57 MB","mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/59322"},{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/59323","id":"59323","filename":"screen-capture - 2026-08-05T123205.802 (09bd7cbc-148e-4a9d-85bf-687acf7f2288).webm","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bilal.muzamil@shopview.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png"},"displayName":"Bilal Muzamil","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Karachi","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"Yesterday 12:32 PM","size":"1.57 MB","mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/59323"}],"summary":null,"creator":null,"subtasks":null,"customfield_10285":"","reporter":null,"customfield_10044":null,"aggregateprogress":null,"customfield_10046":null,"customfield_10047":null,"environment":"","customfield_10318":null,"duedate":null,"customfield_10518":null,"progress":null,"votes":null,"comment":{"comments":[{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/54998/comment/74528","id":"74528","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bil