ame":"To Do"}},"components":[],"timeoriginalestimate":null,"description":{"type":"doc","version":1,"content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Environment"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"QA branch https://sv8785.qa.shopview.com/workorders — build v3.4.2-d00239b (index.html last modified Tue, 04 Aug 2026 22:51:02 GMT). Desktop browser, signed in as an Admin."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steps to Reproduce"}]},{"type":"orderedList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Open Work Orders on the All tab with no filters on."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Click the Customer button and pick the customer named Iibay Landscaping. The button correctly reads \"Customer: Iibay Landscaping\" and the list narrows."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now leave the page and come back — any of these four does it: open a work order and click back; refresh the page; close the browser completely and sign in again; or open the same link in a new window."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Look at the Customer button."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repeat the whole thing with the Lead Technician button (pick Admin ShopView) and with the Service Advisor button (pick Admin ShopView)."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Expected Result"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The button should still read \"Customer: Iibay Landscaping\", the same as it did before you left the page. The user needs to see WHICH customer the list is filtered by without opening the button."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Current Result"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The button comes back blue (switched on) but reads only \"Customer\" — the customer's name is gone. The filter itself is still working: the list is still filtered by that customer, and if you open the button the name is there as a tag with a tick beside it. So the list is filtered by something the screen no longer names."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The same thing happens on the Lead Technician and Service Advisor buttons. It does NOT happen on the Status or Asset on Site buttons — those keep their value (\"Status: Paid\" comes back correctly), so a user sees one button naming its value and another not naming its value side by side."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"How often"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every time, on all four routes back to the page, on all three of those buttons. Reproduced twice from a clean start."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":3},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Technical detail"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The three affected filters are the ones whose choices are fetched from the server (/api/customers/list-options and the staff list); the two unaffected ones are fixed lists held in the page. On a restore the saved filter value is read back and applied to the request (filters[n][field]=company_id&filters[n][value]=00122246-ab6d-47ee-a885-3425c7bda754) but the button's label is rendered before the name for that id is available, and is not re-rendered once it arrives. Specification references: S7-R1, which says the chip \"displays the selected value(s)\", and S10-R1, which says filter selections are \"restored exactly as they were left\"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":" "}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Filters specification, version 18, requirement S7-R1, which says: \"When a filter has one or more values selected, the chip changes to an active/highlighted visual state (blue pill) and displays the selected value(s)\". The last five words are the part that is missing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"And requirement S10-R1, which says: \"When the user navigates away from the Work Orders page (e.g., to a Work Order detail, then back), the filter selections and collapsed/expanded state are restored exactly as they were left\"."}]}]},"customfield_10015":null,"timetracking":{},"security":null,"aggregatetimeestimate":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/59322","id":"59322","filename":"screen-capture - 2026-08-05T123205.802.webm","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bilal.muzamil@shopview.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png"},"displayName":"Bilal Muzamil","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Karachi","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"2026-08-05T02:32:38.229-0500","size":1641939,"mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/59322"},{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/59323","id":"59323","filename":"screen-capture - 2026-08-05T123205.802 (09bd7cbc-148e-4a9d-85bf-687acf7f2288).webm","author":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bilal.muzamil@shopview.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png"},"displayName":"Bilal Muzamil","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Karachi","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"2026-08-05T02:32:43.130-0500","size":1641939,"mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/59323"}],"summary":"A saved Customer, Lead Technician or Service Advisor filter comes back without its name on the button","creator":{"self":"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=712020%3A6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","accountId":"712020:6d590212-5c9b-4135-ae11-277f3826110e","emailAddress":"bilal.muzamil@shopview.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FBM-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/939e0aa31ab923104bfaac4c5012d8c0?d=https%3A%2F%2Favat